Audio Sentinel

The initial application was derived from the OpenVela project source at:
https://github.com/open-vela/contest2026_456_wuheihei
Initial source snapshot: bc01a35c8f9fef636ebaff0e77a5ea75ca21a564

The current release is maintained at:
https://github.com/bilibilidev/audio-sentinel-v11
It contains the formal Tiny MLP implementation, subsequent training and model
export work, board integration, Linux demonstrations and experimental results.
Original copyright and license notices remain applicable to their contents.

Synthetic keyword templates and the MFCC/DTW prototype originate from the
initial application and are retained with their generation code. Their test
results describe synthetic speech rather than independent human recordings.

Datasets, vendor SDKs and firmware binaries, private credentials and original
audio recordings are managed separately. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for resource
attribution and licensing information. The project source license does not
replace the licenses of data, external code or vendor components.
